{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"diff -u src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/siteset.cljc src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc | head -200; rg -n '\"'^'\"\\\\(def' src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc; head -65 src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude{,_p9,_module}.cljc; rg -n 'prelude-p9|prelude-module|prelude\\\\.p9|prelude\\\\.module' src/cljc/yang/php\"","aggregated_output":"--- src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/siteset.cljc\t2026-11-15 01:46:19.583635118 -0500\n+++ src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc\t2026-11-15 01:46:19.586635162 -0500\n@@ -1,85 +1,151 @@\n-(ns yang.php.antlr.siteset\n-  \"Publication of PHP occurrence marks beside canonical module rows.\"\n-  (:require\n-    [dao.jing :as jing]\n-    [yang.safepoint :as safepoint]\n-    [yang.core.module :as core-module]\n-    [yang.core.uast :as u]\n-    [yin.vm.linker.publish :as publish]\n-    [yin.vm :as vm]\n-    [yin.vm.encoder :as encoder]\n-    [yin.vm.linker.sign :as sign]))\n-\n-\n-(def frontend-revision \"yang.php.antlr.lower/sites-1\")\n+(ns yang.python.antlr.siteset\n+  \"C4 slice I7 (docs/design/yang.antlr.md 8.5.6, ruling 14): published site\n+   sets for imported modules.\n+\n+   Site marks never enter canonical rows, so a published module tree\n+   carries none; they live in the frontend-metadata side table. A module's\n+   site set is that side table's `:yang/site` marks for the module tree,\n+   sorted (`yang.safepoint/site-set`) and content-addressed. A separate\n+   publication record, keyed by the module's manifest address, pins the\n+   association: the exact code root (the manifest's `:yin.module/tree`),\n+   the frontend revision, the transformation profile and the set's\n+   address. The module manifest keeps its schema: a manifest address names\n+   code, and a record names a manifest.\n+\n+   Discovery. The publisher signs a publication entry per module,\n+   `{:yang.site/manifest m :yang.site/record record-address ...}`, and\n+   indexes it as the datoms `[e :yang.site/envelope env]` and `[e\n+   :yang.site/proof proof]` beside its name envelopes (`signed-entry`).\n+   A reader `discover`s a manifest's record addresses from the index\n+   datoms it loaded, under the principals it declares; only a declared\n+   principal's signature makes an entry count. The record and the set are\n+   fetched by address and verified against it.\n+\n+   A consumer under a profile requiring hooks `admit`s an import: it\n+   verifies every pin against the published code root and refuses a\n+   missing, empty or mismatched set, naming the profile and the set.\n+   `stage` then applies a verified set at link time, as the linker\n+   composition's `:stage`: it derives the instrumented module `A'` from the\n+   published tree alone, bottom-up over the module's guest requirements,\n+   and publishes it beside its `:derive` record. An explicitly noninterruptible profile imports the module\n+   as published, with none.\"\n+  (:require [dao.jing :as jing]\n+            [yang.python.antlr.lower :as lower]\n+            [yang.safepoint :as safepoint]\n+            [yin.vm :as vm]\n+            [yin.vm.encoder :as encoder]\n+            [yin.vm.linker.publish :as publish]\n+            [yin.vm.linker.sign :as sign]))\n+\n+\n+(def frontend-revision\n+  \"The frontend revision the marks are pinned to: it moves with any change\n+   to which nodes the Python lowering marks, or how.\"\n+  \"yang.python.antlr.lower/sites-1\")\n \n \n (def lowering-profile\n-  {:yang.site/unit :module, :yang.site/prelude :linked,\n+  \"The transformation profile the marks were made under: the module\n+   emitter over the linked prelude, marking these kinds.\"\n+  {:yang.site/unit :module,\n+   :yang.site/prelude :linked,\n    :yang.site/kinds [:call :line :loop]})\n \n \n-(def profile-address (jing/segment-key lowering-profile))\n+(def profile-address\n+  \"The address the transformation profile is pinned by.\"\n+  (jing/segment-key lowering-profile))\n+\n+\n+(defn- medium\n+  []\n+  :yang.python.antlr/site-set)\n \n \n (defn site-set-of\n-  \"The canonical root and occurrence marks of module AST `ast`.\"\n+  \"`{:root address :tree tree :set [[path mark] ...]}` for the module map\n+   AST `ast`: the address of its canonical tree, the tree's rows and its\n+   sorted site set.\"\n   [ast]\n   (let [env (encoder/project (encoder/source-envelope\n-                               :yang.php.antlr/site-set [:site-set 0] [ast]))\n+                               (medium) [:site-set 0] [ast]))\n         tree (nth (:yin/batch env) (:yin/root env))\n         origin (vm/source-origin (:yin/source-medium env)\n                                  (:yin/batch-token env) (:yin/root env))\n         sites (safepoint/sites (:yin/frontend-metadata env) origin (:root tree))]\n-    {:root (:root tree), :set (safepoint/site-set sites)}))\n+    {:root (:root tree), :tree tree, :set (safepoint/site-set sites)}))\n+\n+\n+(defn record\n+  \"The publication record associating manifest `manifest` with site set\n+   `set-address` over code root `root`.\"\n+  [manifest root set-address]\n+  {:yang.site/manifest manifest,\n+   :yang.site/root root,\n+   :yang.site/revision frontend-revision,\n+   :yang.site/profile profile-address,\n+   :yang.site/set set-address})\n \n \n (defn publish!\n-  \"Publish the set, including an empty set, and its manifest/root binding.\"\n+  \"Publish the site set of module `ast` (published at manifest address\n+   `manifest`) into `handle`: the set as one blob, then its record. Answers\n+   `{:record r :record-address a :set-address s :set [...]}`.\"\n   [handle manifest ast]\n   (let [{:keys [root set]} (site-set-of ast)\n         set-address (jing/materialize! handle (vec set))\n-        record {:yang.site/manifest manifest, :yang.site/root root,\n-                :yang.site/revision frontend-revision,\n-                :yang.site/profile profile-address, :yang.site/set set-address}]\n-    {:record record, :record-address (jing/materialize! handle record),\n-     :set-address set-address, :set set}))\n+        r (record manifest root set-address)]\n+    {:record r,\n+     :record-address (jing/materialize! handle r),\n+     :set-address set-address,\n+     :set set}))\n \n \n (defn- read-at\n+  \"The value at `address` in `handle`: `::absent` when the handle holds no\n+   bytes for a segment address (the handle is asked with a not-found\n+   sentinel, as a byte store is), nil when `address` is no segment address\n+   or its bytes do not hash to it, else the value.\"\n   [handle address]\n-  (when (jing/segment-address? address)\n-    (let [bytes ((:get-bytes-fn handle) address ::absent)]\n+  (if-not (jing/segment-address? address)\n+    nil\n+    (let [bs ((:get-bytes-fn handle) address ::absent)]\n       (cond\n-        (or (nil? bytes) (= ::absent bytes)) ::absent\n-        (jing/segment-bytes-match? address bytes) (jing/segment-value address bytes)))))\n+        (= ::absent bs) ::absent\n+        (nil? bs) ::absent\n+        (jing/segment-bytes-match? address bs) (jing/segment-value address bs)\n+        :else nil))))\n \n \n-(defn verify\n-  \"Read and verify a published set, or return nil for missing or mismatched\n-   metadata. An empty set is a valid publication.\"\n-  [handle manifest record-address]\n-  (let [module (read-at handle manifest)\n-        record (read-at handle record-address)\n-        sites (read-at handle (when (map? record) (:yang.site/set record)))]\n-    (when (and (map? module) (map? record) (vector? sites)\n-               (= manifest (:yang.site/manifest record))\n-               (= (:yin.module/tree module) (:yang.site/root record))\n-               (= frontend-revision (:yang.site/revision record))\n-               (= profile-address (:yang.site/profile record))\n-               (every? (fn [entry]\n-                         (and (vector? entry) (= 2 (count entry))\n-                              (vector? (first entry))\n-                              (let [mark (second entry)\n-                                    kind (if (vector? mark) (first mark) mark)]\n-                                (contains? #{:call :line :loop} kind))))\n-                       sites)\n-               (= sites (safepoint/site-set (into {} sites))))\n-      {:record record, :set sites})))\n+(defn- absent?\n+  [x]\n+  (= ::absent x))\n+\n+\n+(defn- missing\n+  \"The stage's report of the absent `address`: first one met, nothing\n+   written.\"\n+  [address]\n+  {:status :missing, :address address})\n+\n \n+(defn- fetch\n+  \"The value at `address` in `handle`, or nil when absent or not its\n+   address.\"\n+  [handle address]\n+  (let [v (read-at handle address)]\n+    (when-not (absent? v) v)))\n+\n+\n+;; =============================================================================\n+;; Discovery\n+;; =============================================================================\n \n (defn signed-entry\n-  \"Sign the association between a published manifest and its site record.\"\n+  \"The publisher `key`'s (`{:seed :public}`) signed publication entry\n+   `{:envelope e :proof p}` for the record at `record-address` of the\n41:(def frontend-revision\n47:(def lowering-profile\n55:(def profile-address\n60:(defn- medium\n65:(defn site-set-of\n79:(defn record\n90:(defn publish!\n104:(defn- read-at\n120:(defn- absent?\n125:(defn- missing\n132:(defn- fetch\n144:(defn signed-entry\n157:(defn entry-datoms\n166:(defn discover\n197:(defn- refusal\n207:(defn- entry-ok?\n219:(defn verify\n254:(defn admit\n310:(defn- load-tree\n339:(defn- derive-module\n406:(defn- records-for\n414:(defn- derive-closure\n459:(defn- overlay\n494:(def reasons\n502:(defn stage\n541:(defn signed-entries\n==> src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc <==\n(ns ^{:clj-kondo/config '{:lint-as {yang.php.antlr.quoted/defquoted clojure.core/def}}}\n yang.php.antlr.prelude\n  \"The PHP runtime profile, written as Universal AST\n   (docs/design/yang.php.md sections 3.5, 7, 9). PHP semantics for operators,\n   juggling, comparison, output and errors live here as guest code, not in\n   Clojure: the lowering only emits applications of these names.\n\n   Value encoding (P1):\n     int             host integer in [-2^63, 2^63-1] (a BigInt carrier on JS\n                     past 2^53); every operator computes the exact result\n                     through the `integer` module and demotes to float when\n                     it leaves the range\n     float           untagged Jing float64 content (`data/float64`), the\n                     shared ruling of yang.typescript.md section 2; the kind\n                     test is `php/kind`, never a second tag. The prelude\n                     holds no integral float literal (JS reads 1.0 as 1):\n                     floats are built with `data/float64` or computed, and\n                     host arithmetic only ever sees `data/float-value`\n     string          a host string whose every char is one byte (a latin-1\n                     carrier); the lowering resolves literal text to bytes\n     bool            host true / false\n     null            :php/null\n     array           {:php/type :array :index {key value} :order [key ...]\n                     :next-index n}: a persistent ordered map; keys are\n                     ints or strings (`php/array-key`); `:next-index` is\n                     absent until the first integer key is written\n     error object    {:php/type :obj :class name :ord n :props {\\\"message\\\"\n                     \\\"code\\\" \\\"previous\\\"}}\n     function        a cell {:php/type :function :name s :code (fn [args])\n                             :yang.call/entry (fn [invocation])}\n\n   Runtime state is allocated by `php/init!`, once per task, under the slot\n   `php.rt/state` (the literal `:php/uninit` until `php/init!` flips it to\n   `:php/ready` as its last write):\n     php.rt/ctx            the dynamic context {:handlers :depth :base :frame}\n     php.rt/out            a cell holding the buffer stack, a vector of\n                           buffers, each a vector of byte-string chunks;\n                           `php/echo` conjs onto the last buffer, the\n                           bottom buffer is never popped\n     php.rt/globals        a cell holding the plain array of section 10.1\n                           (`$GLOBALS`), `(php/empty-array)` initially\n     php.rt/functions      a cell holding a map of lower-cased name to\n                           function cell; builtins are pre-seeded\n     php.rt/classes        a cell holding a map of class name to class record\n                           (the Throwable hierarchy, data only)\n     php.rt/next-ord       a cell, the per-task object ordinal\n     php.rt/next-cell      a cell, the per-task counted-cell id (`:id`)\n     php.rt/request        a cell holding the explicit request record\n     php.rt/response       a cell holding ordered response records\n                           (compositions without streams)\n     php.rt/response-stream, php.rt/diag-stream\n                           cells holding the composition-supplied stream\n                           references execution emits response and\n                           diagnostic records on, :php/null without them\n     php.rt/headers-sent, php.rt/status   output state and the response status\n     php.rt/error-handler  a cell, :php/null or a callable\n     php.rt/error-handlers a cell holding previous handlers for restoration\n     php.rt/error-reporting a cell, the mask (E_ALL initially)\n     php.rt/diag           a cell, the vector of diagnostic records\n     php.rt/int-max, php.rt/int-min   exact integers computed in `init!`,\n                           never literals (literals past 2^53 are not\n                           portable)\n\n   Errors are raised with `php/raise`; with no handler frame above them they\n   reach the unit root, `php/run-main`, which answers output, response and\n\n==> src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude_p9.cljc <==\n(ns ^{:clj-kondo/config '{:lint-as {yang.php.antlr.quoted/defquoted clojure.core/def}}}\n yang.php.antlr.prelude-p9\n  \"P9 string, array, JSON and math builtins, written as guest code.\"\n  (:require\n    #?(:cljd [clojure.edn :as edn])\n    [yang.php.antlr.quoted :refer [defquoted]]))\n\n\n(defquoted ^:private forms\n  \"P9 definitions in dependency order.\"\n  '[[php/p9-string\n     (fn [v] (php/to-string v))]\n    [php/p9-substr\n     (fn [s start length]\n       (let [n (data/str-length s)\n             a (if (< start 0) (if (> (+ n start) 0) (+ n start) 0) start)\n             a (if (> a n) n a)\n             b (if (= length :php/null)\n                 n\n                 (if (< length 0) (+ n length) (+ a length)))\n             b (if (< b a) a (if (> b n) n b))]\n         (if (>= a n) \"\" (data/substring s a b))))]\n    [php/bi-substr\n     (fn [args]\n       (do (php/arity-between \"substr\" args 2 3 \"at least 2\")\n           (php/p9-substr (php/p9-string (get args 0)) (php/to-int (get args 1))\n                          (php/arg-or args 2 :php/null))))]\n    [php/p9-index-of\n     (fn [h needle from insensitive]\n       (let [h (if insensitive (php/lc h) h) needle (if insensitive (php/lc needle) needle)\n             nh (data/str-length h) nn (data/str-length needle)]\n         (php/p9-index-loop h needle from (- nh nn) nn)))]\n    [php/p9-index-loop\n     (fn [h needle i last nn]\n       (if (> i last)\n         false\n         (if (= nn 0) i\n             (if (= (data/substring h i (+ i nn)) needle)\n               i (php/p9-index-loop h needle (+ i 1) last nn)))))]\n    [php/p9-strpos\n     (fn [name args insensitive]\n       (do (php/arity-between name args 2 3 \"at least 2\")\n           (php/p9-index-of (php/p9-string (get args 0)) (php/p9-string (get args 1))\n                            (php/to-int (php/arg-or args 2 0)) insensitive)))]\n    [php/bi-strpos (fn [args] (php/p9-strpos \"strpos\" args false))]\n    [php/bi-stripos (fn [args] (php/p9-strpos \"stripos\" args true))]\n    [php/p9-rindex-loop\n     ;; the rightmost match at or above lo, at or below the starting i\n     (fn [h needle i nn lo]\n       (if (< i lo) false\n           (if (= (data/substring h i (+ i nn)) needle) i\n               (php/p9-rindex-loop h needle (- i 1) nn lo))))]\n    [php/bi-strrpos\n     ;; a non-negative offset is the search's lower bound (searching back\n     ;; from the end); a negative one starts that many characters from the\n     ;; end and searches back from there; out-of-range offsets are a\n     ;; ValueError, like PHP 8\n     (fn [args]\n       (do (php/arity-between \"strrpos\" args 2 3 \"at least 2\")\n           (let [h (php/p9-string (get args 0)) n (php/p9-string (get args 1))\n                 nn (data/str-length n) len (data/str-length h)\n                 off (php/to-int (php/arg-or args 2 0))]\n             (if (= n \"\")\n               (php/throw-error \"ValueError\" \"strrpos(): Argument #2 ($needle) must not be empty\")\n               (if (if (> off len) true (< off (integer/neg len)))\n\n==> src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude_module.cljc <==\n(ns ^{:clj-kondo/config '{:lint-as {yang.php.antlr.quoted/defquoted clojure.core/def}}}\n yang.php.antlr.prelude-module\n  \"The include/require runtime of the PHP profile (docs/design/yang.php.md\n   section 11, plan P6 R3/R4): the four kinds, the `_once` check, the two\n   missing stages. Guest code like the rest of the prelude; the lowering\n   emits only applications of these names.\n\n   Runtime state `php/init!` allocates for it (prelude.cljc owns the keys):\n     php.rt/included   a cell, map of normalized path to true; written on\n                       `:ok` delivery only, never on a refusal\n     php.rt/unit       a cell, the executing unit's path or :php/null\n     php.rt/path-map   a cell, map of normalized path to a delivery thunk\n                       (the literal path map of the composition's `:paths`)\"\n  (:require\n    #?(:cljd [clojure.edn :as edn])\n    [yang.php.antlr.quoted :refer [defquoted]]))\n\n\n(def include-path-text\n  \"The `include_path` the missing-include texts print: the oracle image's\n   default. PENDING the S0 oracle pin (php:8.3-cli reports\n   `.:/usr/local/lib/php`).\"\n  \".:/usr/local/lib/php\")\n\n\n(def include-kinds\n  \"The four kinds the lowering passes to `php/include-run`.\"\n  #{:include :include-once :require :require-once})\n\n\n(defquoted ^:private module-forms\n  \"The include definitions, `[store-key form]`.\"\n  '[[php/include-kind-name\n     (fn [kind]\n       (if (= kind :include)\n         \"include\"\n         (if (= kind :include-once)\n           \"include_once\"\n           (if (= kind :require) \"require\" \"require_once\"))))]\n    [php/include-require?\n     (fn [kind] (if (= kind :require) true (= kind :require-once)))]\n    [php/include-once?\n     (fn [kind] (if (= kind :include-once) true (= kind :require-once)))]\n    [php/warn-refusal\n     ;; php/warn with the structured refusal on the record (plan R4)\n     (fn [errno msg refusal]\n       (let [rec (assoc (php/warn-record errno msg) :yang.php/refusal refusal)\n             h (cell/get php.rt/error-handler)]\n         (if (= h :php/null)\n           (php/warn-sink rec)\n           (if (= (php/invoke-handler h errno msg) false)\n             (php/warn-sink rec)\n             :php/null))))]\n    [php/include-missing!\n     ;; the refusal map follows the base kind; the texts carry the kind as\n     ;; written; a refused path is never marked included\n     (fn [path kind refusal]\n       (let [nm (php/include-kind-name kind)]\n         (do (php/warn-refusal\n               2\n               (data/str-concat\n                 (data/str-concat (data/str-concat nm \"(\") path)\n                 \"): Failed to open stream: No such file or directory\")\n               refusal)\n             (if (php/include-require? kind)\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude_module.cljc:2: yan