ll definitions must precede every Python call,\n-   just as in the bundled prelude.\"\n+  \"The linked safepointed run's tree: `js` required and initialized, `jssp`\n+   required, the signal stream the composition bound under `signals-key`\n+   attached, then the derived linked program `a'`, whose own require and\n+   init are idempotent re-entries. The load order is the linked one, the\n+   inverse of the bundled hook-prelude-first order.\"\n   [a']\n   (u/mark-tails\n     (u/seq-nodes\n-      [(u/sexp->uast '(require (quote yang.call)))\n-       (u/sexp->uast (list 'require (list 'quote prelude/module-name)))\n+      [(u/sexp->uast (list 'require (list 'quote prelude/module-name)))\n        (u/sexp->uast (list 'require (list 'quote module-name)))\n-       (u/sexp->uast '(py/init!))\n+       (u/sexp->uast '(js/init!))\n        (u/app (u/v (symbol (name module-name) \"attach!\")) (u/v signals-key))\n        a'])))\n \n \n ;; =============================================================================\n-;; The module emitter: the same definition list as the linker module `pysp`\n+;; The module emitter: the same definition list as the linker module `jssp`\n ;; =============================================================================\n \n (def runtime-keys\n-  \"Every key `pysp/attach!` defines, sorted: the handler cell, the\n-   signal cursor and the trace cell. Each is a runtime key of the module, held at install\n-   time by a `:py/uninit` placeholder so the linker's scanners discharge\n-   the bodies that read it.\"\n-  '[py.sp/handler py.sp/cursor py.sp/trace])\n+  \"Every key `jssp/attach!` defines, sorted: the signal cursor. It is held\n+   at install time by a `:js/uninit` placeholder so the linker's scanners\n+   discharge the bodies that read it.\"\n+  '[js.sp/cursor])\n \n \n (defn strip\n-  \"`sym` without the module's own namespace `py.sp`; any other value as it\n-   is. `py/*` stays qualified: those are the base prelude's exports,\n-   resolved through the registry once `py` is linked, and stripping them\n+  \"`sym` without the module's own namespace `js.sp`; any other value as it\n+   is. `js/*` stays qualified: those are the base prelude's exports,\n+   resolved through the registry once `js` is linked, and stripping them\n    would collide with this module's own bare keys.\"\n   [sym]\n-  (core/strip \"py.sp\" sym))\n+  (core/strip \"js.sp\" sym))\n \n \n (def ^:private module-definitions\n-  \"The module's definition list: a `:py/uninit` placeholder for every\n+  \"The module's definition list: a `:js/uninit` placeholder for every\n    runtime key, so each read of one is discharged by an unconditional\n    module-level definition, then every definition, stripped.\"\n-  (core/module-definitions \"py.sp\" :py/uninit runtime-keys function-definitions))\n+  (core/module-definitions \"js.sp\" :js/uninit runtime-keys function-definitions))\n \n \n (def module-uast\n   \"The module tree: one application whose operands define hooks, then\n    deliver the pinned base prelude, applied to a lambda returning nil.\n-   Every definition precedes every call, including require, so the\n-   linker's scanners discharge sibling and runtime-key reads. Defining\n-   runs nothing; delivery never initializes either runtime.\"\n-  (core/module-tree module-definitions [(u/sexp->uast '(require (quote py)))]))\n+   Every definition precedes every call, including require, so the linker's\n+   scanners discharge sibling and runtime-key reads. Defining runs nothing;\n+   delivery never initializes either runtime. C1 finalized, like every\n+   published production tree: its `:yang/call-site` markers publish beside\n+   its manifest (see `yin.vm.linker.publish`), never inside it, so the\n+   manifest keeps schema 1 and its address does not move.\"\n+  (u/annotate-call-sites\n+    (core/module-tree module-definitions\n+                      [(u/sexp->uast '(require (quote js)))])))\n \n \n (def module-exports\n-  \"The module's exports: ev